WEBVTT

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:19.642
Immortal Man

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:29.651
Swietokrzyskie Mountains,
Eastern Poland

00:01:30.357 --> 00:01:33.693
I hope the engine doesn't
give out here.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.329
I must reach Krakow before
the sun goes down.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.763
I'm counting on you, ole girl.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.279
You all right?!

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.986
Any injuries?

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.021
Fool.

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:02.789
Why don't you look
where you're going?

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.781
You could've easily
killed someone.

00:02:07.027 --> 00:02:09.723
If I weren't immortal, I'd be dead.

00:02:10.931 --> 00:02:11.955
Right...

00:02:17.771 --> 00:02:19.639
What a disappointing car.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.641
The heater hardly works.

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.376
It's awfully cold in here.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.878
I'm very sorry.

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:27.938
It's a rental, so hang in there
until we reach the city.

00:02:28.782 --> 00:02:31.012
Oh, right.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:35.587
How about some of this?

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.191
Some brandy, huh?

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:42.719
You want me to drink this
cheap crap to warm up?

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:45.432
Sorry about that.

00:02:45.432 --> 00:02:46.990
It's the best I can do.

00:02:54.341 --> 00:02:57.037
Can't you go any faster?

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.578
I can see you're in a rush.

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.978
But this is the fastest it'll go.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.461
Stop, now!

00:03:14.461 --> 00:03:15.795
Pull over!

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:16.830
Ignore them.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:18.031
Keep driving.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:18.463
Wha...?

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.933
Semionov!

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:22.333
Return our money,
you con artist!

00:03:22.702 --> 00:03:26.439
How rude of him to call me
a con artist, huh?

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:27.770
How dare he.

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.645
I can see you, Semionov!

00:03:32.645 --> 00:03:34.340
What do you have to say for yourself?!

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.680
Wh-What're you going to do?

00:03:40.487 --> 00:03:41.181
There!

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:55.335
Pathetic men.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.270
That wouldn't have
happened to them...

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.034
...if they had had a little foresight.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.008
What do you mean?

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:04.511
But how? You're the one who...

00:04:04.511 --> 00:04:06.079
Yes, thanks to me...

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.913
...they got to enjoy that
most thrilling moment.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:14.081
Life is not life if one hasn't
experienced its thrills.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:16.122
Wouldn't you agree?

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.282
Young man?

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.593
Uh, I'm Keaton. Taichi Keaton.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.095
An agent for the insurance industry.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.586
And I'm Andrei Semionov.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:27.167
Oh. So, you're Russian?

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.067
Were they as well?

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:29.736
Yes.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.404
They used to work for the KGB.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:33.840
But now they're Russian Mafia.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.068
Russian Mafia!?

00:04:35.809 --> 00:04:39.446
They don't know the first thing
about enjoying life.

00:04:39.446 --> 00:04:41.073
A bunch of idiots.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:44.951
People had hopes for the country
after the fall of the Soviet Union...

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:47.720
...but when I returned from
my exile in America...

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.423
...the country was in terrible shape.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:53.326
Like a sick patient on the very
verge of death.

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:57.524
I mean, really. Even the borscht
in Moscow was as bad as it gets.

00:04:57.931 --> 00:05:01.167
I can't accept a Russia
with such bad borscht.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.135
You'll see.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:06.639
I'll be the one to bring back
real borscht to Russia.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.475
Uh, by the way...

00:05:08.475 --> 00:05:11.205
...why are you involved
with the Russian Mafia?

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:15.181
Well, I suppose you could say
it's a matter of showing them...

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.783
...the simple pleasures in life.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:19.217
I'm what you would call
their teacher.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:20.787
Teacher?

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:21.913
Is that right?

00:05:32.565 --> 00:05:34.590
Come on out, Semionov!

00:05:36.069 --> 00:05:37.637
Give us the money!

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.696
Or prepare to take
your last breath!

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:41.808
Money, money, money...

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.576
That's all they want.

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:46.179
All over a mere 100,000 dollars.

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.441
100,000 dollars?

00:05:47.981 --> 00:05:50.216
Look at their faces.

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:53.652
See how money can
make a man so ugly.

00:06:00.226 --> 00:06:01.661
All right, all right!

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:03.288
I'm coming out!

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:04.894
Just keep it down!
All that noise.

00:06:10.637 --> 00:06:13.299
Well, Keaton. Let's step out.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:17.510
Good.

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.909
It's about time.

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.181
It's really too bad.

00:06:21.181 --> 00:06:23.049
If you had given me
a little more time...

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:27.349
...you would have got your hands
on some real riches.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.356
Keaton...

00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:32.091
...you said you were an agent.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.994
I hope that means you're
accustomed to danger.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.428
Uh, well. Not too often.

00:06:38.231 --> 00:06:39.199
Right.

00:06:39.199 --> 00:06:41.133
Then, you may learn something.

00:06:42.202 --> 00:06:44.571
Let's have some good fun.

00:06:44.571 --> 00:06:45.902
With this danger.

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:47.134
What?

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.170
Well, let's go, Keaton.

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:53.136
Hey, come back!

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.567
We did it, Keaton.

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:18.130
How's that?! Let that be a lesson!

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:30.984
This stupid snow is
as bad as junk mail.

00:07:30.984 --> 00:07:34.420
Keeps on coming even though
you don't want it.

00:07:34.988 --> 00:07:39.158
But it was the snow that saved
your country from people like...

00:07:39.158 --> 00:07:40.493
...Napoleon and Hitler.

00:07:40.493 --> 00:07:42.095
Exactly right.

00:07:42.095 --> 00:07:44.620
But it wasn't just the snow
that saved my mother country.

00:07:44.998 --> 00:07:47.500
A lot of blood was shed.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:51.638
But snow could also
cover up all that blood.

00:07:51.638 --> 00:07:53.299
Snow sure can be...

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:02.546
...a damn nuisance...

00:08:07.086 --> 00:08:08.849
I'm sorry.

00:08:13.159 --> 00:08:14.260
Let's hurry.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.353
The weather's getting worse.

00:08:20.767 --> 00:08:24.470
The blizzard came because
of the terrible things I said...

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:25.738
...about the snow.

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:27.974
Those guys will have
trouble following us now.

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:31.967
That is, if we can make it
into a town.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.514
Don't be so pessimistic.

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:36.573
It'll let up soon enough.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:40.386
No, this blizzard's going
to last a while!

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:43.856
We should rest here in order to
avoid using up our strength!

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:46.959
I don't plan to sit around here!

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:50.759
Vodka and warm women
are waiting for us in town!

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.926
Hey! Wait for me, Mr. Semionov!

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.541
Damned disgusting snow...

00:09:01.541 --> 00:09:04.339
Is it trying to test me?

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:07.213
I am immortal.

00:09:07.213 --> 00:09:08.815
I won't lose.

00:09:08.815 --> 00:09:10.442
I refuse to.

00:09:33.206 --> 00:09:35.071
How do you feel now?

00:09:35.475 --> 00:09:38.376
It appears that you saved my life.

00:09:38.611 --> 00:09:41.637
Not me, but this snow
that you hated so much.

00:09:43.483 --> 00:09:47.620
Snow can hold quite a lot of air
among its crystals.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:50.589
And that air can retain heat.

00:09:51.124 --> 00:09:55.083
But there's another reason
we were saved.

00:09:55.461 --> 00:09:57.986
It's because I am immortal.

00:10:01.134 --> 00:10:03.736
Is the blizzard letting up yet?

00:10:03.736 --> 00:10:06.261
No. Oh, have this.

00:10:06.639 --> 00:10:07.333
Chocolate.

00:10:08.307 --> 00:10:10.969
I forgot I had it in my pocket.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:15.681
But what about you?

00:10:15.681 --> 00:10:16.616
I'm okay.

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:19.380
It's cheap quality.
I hope it's to your satisfaction.

00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:22.648
Guess I'll try.

00:10:26.659 --> 00:10:27.717
It's good.

00:10:29.796 --> 00:10:33.833
It seems I'm now quite
indebted to you because of this.

00:10:33.833 --> 00:10:35.027
Not at all.

00:10:36.636 --> 00:10:39.332
How can I repay you...?

00:10:41.107 --> 00:10:42.074
All right.

00:10:42.675 --> 00:10:46.345
I don't have anything too
extraordinary to offer you.

00:10:46.345 --> 00:10:49.348
But I'd gladly make these
long, dull hours here...

00:10:49.348 --> 00:10:51.384
...a lot more interesting.

00:10:51.384 --> 00:10:51.873
How?

00:10:52.652 --> 00:10:57.089
I have a story about some treasure
beyond anything imaginable.

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:58.420
T-Treasure?

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:01.483
Yes. Treasure.

00:11:05.798 --> 00:11:07.197
Secret treasure?

00:11:08.201 --> 00:11:09.869
Sounds interesting.

00:11:09.869 --> 00:11:11.598
I'd love to hear about it.

00:11:13.606 --> 00:11:17.243
Are you familiar with
Nicholas II?

00:11:17.243 --> 00:11:18.211
Yes.

00:11:18.211 --> 00:11:20.771
The last Czar of the
Russian Empire, right?

00:11:21.614 --> 00:11:23.182
In 1918...

00:11:23.182 --> 00:11:28.279
...he and his family were executed
in Siberia by Lenin's troops.

00:11:28.788 --> 00:11:32.625
Your answer shows you know
much for an insurance man.

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:34.393
Uh, well...

00:11:34.393 --> 00:11:37.330
I used to study some
history and archaeology.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:41.634
You know the estimate
of the fortune he left behind?

00:11:41.634 --> 00:11:43.769
Yes, the Romanovs are
believed to have...

00:11:43.769 --> 00:11:47.106
...accumulated something
like eight billion dollars.

00:11:47.106 --> 00:11:47.940
That's correct.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.209
Platinum and bonds.

00:11:50.209 --> 00:11:52.905
But most exciting of all
is the 500 tons of gold.

00:11:53.613 --> 00:11:56.749
However, during the confusion
after the revolution...

00:11:56.749 --> 00:11:59.585
...the gold was shipped east,
and is still missing today.

00:11:59.585 --> 00:12:03.453
It's said to be tucked away
somewhere in Siberia.

00:12:05.124 --> 00:12:07.393
There are many other
theories about it.

00:12:07.393 --> 00:12:11.497
Like the crazy story that the
Japanese army discovered it...

00:12:11.497 --> 00:12:14.057
...and used it as capital
for Manchuria.

00:12:15.668 --> 00:12:18.771
Greedy people with poor
imaginations come up...

00:12:18.771 --> 00:12:21.107
...with those ridiculous stories.

00:12:21.107 --> 00:12:22.233
Right...

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:27.407
All those theories assume that
the gold was taken to the east.

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:29.482
However...

00:12:29.482 --> 00:12:33.145
...what about the idea that
it was shipped west?

00:12:33.719 --> 00:12:34.887
To the west?

00:12:34.887 --> 00:12:37.223
But it was around the
middle of World War I.

00:12:37.223 --> 00:12:40.954
The Germans had occupied
the Western part of Russia.

00:12:42.728 --> 00:12:45.663
I'm glad that this is
entertaining you.

00:12:46.532 --> 00:12:48.401
A baron who was a subject
of Nicholas II.

00:12:48.401 --> 00:12:51.393
Prince Nikita Volkonsky.

00:12:52.605 --> 00:12:56.776
In the fall of 1916, there was
concern that the revolution...

00:12:56.776 --> 00:13:00.913
...as well as German expansion
would mean the end of the Czar.

00:13:00.913 --> 00:13:02.938
The Czar gave him
a top-secret mission.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:08.880
He was to ship the
500 tons of gold to England.

00:13:09.956 --> 00:13:11.514
But why to England?

00:13:12.959 --> 00:13:13.993
Of course!

00:13:13.993 --> 00:13:15.995
The King of England
was George V...

00:13:15.995 --> 00:13:18.293
...who happened to be
the cousin of Nicholas II.

00:13:18.431 --> 00:13:19.898
That's right.

00:13:20.333 --> 00:13:23.536
The Czar prepared for
two possibilities.

00:13:23.536 --> 00:13:26.699
One, if the Germans
captured Russia...

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:29.966
...he'd use his assets to form
a government within England.

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:32.311
And two...

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:35.247
...if the revolutionaries
jailed them...

00:13:35.247 --> 00:13:37.717
...he could buy his own release.

00:13:37.717 --> 00:13:38.877
Yes, of course.

00:13:39.785 --> 00:13:44.390
Volkonsky managed to ship the
treasure out of St. Petersburg.

00:13:44.390 --> 00:13:47.426
He slipped out of
the port of Arkhangelsk...

00:13:47.426 --> 00:13:49.362
...and headed toward England...

00:13:49.362 --> 00:13:51.353
...while avoiding German attacks.

00:13:52.264 --> 00:13:57.303
Despite all the icebergs
and the heavy fog...

00:13:57.303 --> 00:13:59.505
...he kept pressing
on toward England...

00:13:59.505 --> 00:14:02.742
...no matter what stood
in his way!

00:14:02.742 --> 00:14:03.436
Right.

00:14:04.176 --> 00:14:08.047
Tell me what you think
gave him the greatest fear.

00:14:08.047 --> 00:14:08.911
Well...

00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:12.873
Back then, the German's navy
had control of the sea.

00:14:13.953 --> 00:14:15.921
Of course! The U-boats!

00:14:16.422 --> 00:14:18.324
Exactly.

00:14:18.324 --> 00:14:23.095
The first U-boat put into
active service took to the sea...

00:14:23.095 --> 00:14:27.395
...and threatened the English and
Russian's navies with a new terror.

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:40.413
One report said that U-boats
had succeeded in sinking...

00:14:40.413 --> 00:14:44.042
...800 ships in only three months.

00:14:45.084 --> 00:14:47.143
Was his ship attacked by a U-boat?

00:14:48.888 --> 00:14:50.756
If the story was that simple...

00:14:50.756 --> 00:14:53.793
...it wouldn't be worth telling you
as payment for the chocolate.

00:14:53.793 --> 00:14:56.057
Then, what happened to that ship?!

00:14:56.495 --> 00:14:58.156
Take it easy.

00:15:01.333 --> 00:15:03.069
The sixth day after embarking...

00:15:03.069 --> 00:15:06.470
...when they were about
250 miles from Norway...

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:10.443
...a lookout spotted the dark
shadow of a vessel closing in...

00:15:10.443 --> 00:15:12.172
...through a break in the thick fog.

00:15:19.118 --> 00:15:20.517
Was it a U-boat?

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:22.914
The men thought the same thing.

00:15:23.289 --> 00:15:26.659
So Prince Volkonsky ordered the
helmsman to turn the ship round...

00:15:26.659 --> 00:15:28.752
...in an attempt to
avoid the U-boat.

00:15:47.246 --> 00:15:50.182
It was too late by the time
they noticed.

00:15:50.182 --> 00:15:53.242
The ship hit an iceberg
and was split in two.

00:15:53.686 --> 00:15:56.211
It went to the bottom,
along with the treasure.

00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:00.726
Prince Volkonsky looked
towards the black shadow...

00:16:00.726 --> 00:16:04.355
...as it rose to the surface
directly before him.

00:16:05.564 --> 00:16:06.496
It was the U-boat!

00:16:06.966 --> 00:16:07.830
No!

00:16:19.512 --> 00:16:22.174
It was an enormous
humpback whale.

00:16:24.416 --> 00:16:26.350
I-It was a whale?

00:16:28.087 --> 00:16:29.054
Yes.

00:16:29.555 --> 00:16:32.424
From the very beginning...

00:16:32.424 --> 00:16:34.790
...there were no U-boats
in the area.

00:16:35.928 --> 00:16:38.464
Are you trying to tell me that...

00:16:38.464 --> 00:16:41.000
...if that whale hadn't appeared...

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.768
...the gold would've
made it to England...

00:16:42.768 --> 00:16:44.970
...Nicholas II might have lived...

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:49.275
...and the history of Russia would
have been completely different?

00:16:49.275 --> 00:16:51.072
That's exactly it.

00:16:53.846 --> 00:16:56.280
So, what happened to
Prince Volkonsky?

00:16:56.715 --> 00:16:59.985
Fortunately, he was rescued
by a Norwegian fishing boat.

00:16:59.985 --> 00:17:03.421
He went back to St. Petersburg
where he eventually died.

00:17:03.689 --> 00:17:06.826
But not before leaving behind
a detailed navigation log...

00:17:06.826 --> 00:17:09.226
...to his young son.

00:17:10.596 --> 00:17:12.965
Nikita's wife and child
set off on foot...

00:17:12.965 --> 00:17:16.093
...and went east to
avoid the revolution.

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:19.605
But they were embroiled
in Russia's civil war.

00:17:19.605 --> 00:17:23.769
And the mother died after they
got caught in a blizzard in Siberia.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.911
The son became an orphan...

00:17:25.911 --> 00:17:29.415
...and was sent to China
like the other refugees.

00:17:29.415 --> 00:17:32.051
He ended up with the Red Cross
in Hong Kong...

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:34.212
...and was sent off to America.

00:17:38.624 --> 00:17:42.116
But I just don't understand
how you came upon this story.

00:17:42.928 --> 00:17:44.797
Well, you see...

00:17:44.797 --> 00:17:45.627
Well?

00:17:47.600 --> 00:17:48.726
It's a secret.

00:17:59.511 --> 00:18:02.139
We're almost in town, Keaton.

00:18:02.982 --> 00:18:06.185
Have a drink with me and I'll
tell you more interesting stories?

00:18:06.185 --> 00:18:07.277
S-Sure...

00:18:19.865 --> 00:18:21.662
Stay down, Mr. Semionov!

00:18:22.968 --> 00:18:25.664
Them again.
What a nuisance they are.

00:18:26.105 --> 00:18:27.406
Semionov!

00:18:27.406 --> 00:18:31.638
How dare you swindle money
from us with that phony story!

00:18:32.378 --> 00:18:34.280
If you think it's phony...

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:35.406
...you're a fool!

00:18:35.614 --> 00:18:36.815
Don't play stupid with us!

00:18:36.815 --> 00:18:41.020
We know that you're reputed
to be a professional con artist!

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.421
Just give us back the 100 grand!

00:18:45.557 --> 00:18:48.458
I already spent the money!

00:18:48.861 --> 00:18:49.828
What?!

00:18:50.696 --> 00:18:52.960
They're on the
left side of the hill.

00:18:53.365 --> 00:18:55.267
Who cares if they're left or right?

00:18:55.267 --> 00:18:58.804
In a flat field like this,
there's no way we can escape.

00:18:58.804 --> 00:19:00.533
Both of us will be shot.

00:19:00.906 --> 00:19:05.400
I think I owe you more than
a good story for that chocolate.

00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:08.041
No, don't stand up!

00:19:08.681 --> 00:19:09.581
Hey!

00:19:09.581 --> 00:19:11.550
Over this way!

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.153
This man has nothing to do with this!

00:19:14.153 --> 00:19:16.417
Go on, take your best shot!

00:19:16.822 --> 00:19:18.057
Mr. Semionov!

00:19:18.057 --> 00:19:20.292
But if you do shoot me dead...

00:19:20.292 --> 00:19:23.591
...the secret of the treasure
will be lost forever!

00:19:36.375 --> 00:19:37.774
Mr. Semionov!

00:19:38.577 --> 00:19:39.979
Excellent job.

00:19:39.979 --> 00:19:42.548
Right through the heart.

00:19:42.548 --> 00:19:44.016
He had it coming.

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:44.983
The swindler.

00:19:45.484 --> 00:19:50.717
Swindling money out of us with
that ridiculous Romanov story.

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:53.015
He shouldn't have played
such a dangerous game.

00:19:53.826 --> 00:19:55.157
Why'd you do it?

00:19:55.894 --> 00:20:00.092
You laid your life on the line
all for some cheap chocolate.

00:20:01.333 --> 00:20:03.733
Your cooked-up story
was good enough.

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.960
I really enjoyed it.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:11.571
Cheap, but it was very tasty.

00:20:13.812 --> 00:20:14.779
Huh?

00:20:19.118 --> 00:20:20.642
Mr. Semionov?

00:20:22.621 --> 00:20:26.250
B-But how'd you survive
a bullet to the heart?

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:29.157
Somehow I'm still alive.

00:20:34.199 --> 00:20:35.334
This is it!

00:20:35.334 --> 00:20:37.029
This diary saved your life!

00:20:38.837 --> 00:20:41.271
Then, my father protected me.

00:20:42.041 --> 00:20:43.269
Your father?

00:20:45.077 --> 00:20:49.036
Diary...
Nikita A. Volkonsky.

00:20:50.883 --> 00:20:52.248
Nikita?!

00:20:55.354 --> 00:20:56.588
Don't tell me...

00:20:56.588 --> 00:20:57.919
...Mr. Semionov...

00:20:58.424 --> 00:21:00.324
Are you the son of
Prince Volkonsky?

00:21:02.728 --> 00:21:04.329
I already told you.

00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:05.023
Huh?

00:21:05.998 --> 00:21:08.523
That I'm immortal.

00:21:13.205 --> 00:21:16.038
Life is nothing without its thrills!

00:21:16.375 --> 00:21:18.277
Don't you think, Keaton?

00:21:18.277 --> 00:21:19.505
Y-Yes.

00:21:19.711 --> 00:21:23.348
I've paid my debt.
How about we have those drinks?

00:21:23.348 --> 00:21:25.684
But it'll have to be your treat.

00:21:25.684 --> 00:21:27.982
I'm running a little short on cash.

00:21:31.356 --> 00:21:34.860
What exactly did you do with
the money you got from them?

00:21:34.860 --> 00:21:36.295
Well!

00:21:36.295 --> 00:21:40.493
I have another interesting story
about that very thing!

00:21:53.812 --> 00:22:04.590
In a dream I had,
I noticed your distant, faint voice

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:11.962
A scene so familiar
playing out in reality

00:22:12.731 --> 00:22:15.632
In my consciousness

00:22:17.002 --> 00:22:24.943
The sky I was searching for
brings forth a gentleness

00:22:24.943 --> 00:22:28.970
Time will give me the answer

00:22:35.320 --> 00:22:40.893
In the blank scene before me

00:22:40.893 --> 00:22:46.565
I walk as the wind blows

00:22:46.565 --> 00:22:53.906
I just want to touch it
with my own hands

00:22:53.906 --> 00:23:00.778
As the wind blows against me

00:23:07.452 --> 00:23:11.218
How much can one learn
during one's lifetime?

00:23:11.757 --> 00:23:13.559
As long as you have the passion...

00:23:13.559 --> 00:23:16.119
...you can educate yourself
no matter where you are.

00:23:16.828 --> 00:23:19.023
That is what he taught us.

00:23:19.831 --> 00:23:22.634
As long as there is a place
where people can gather...

00:23:22.634 --> 00:23:25.337
...no matter how
chaotic the situation...

00:23:25.337 --> 00:23:28.864
...one can always gain
from education.

00:23:29.708 --> 00:23:32.044
Paris Under the Roof
Next time... Paris Under the Roof

00:23:32.044 --> 00:23:33.671
Paris Under the Roof
